language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Revenue maximisation: choose how many units of each itinerary package to sell so that the seats reserved on each flight leg stay within its capacity, and total revenue is as large as possible.
given demand_dim1 : int
letting n_packages = demand_dim1
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_packages)] of int
given revenue : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_packages)] of int
given available_seats_dim1 : int
letting n_legs = available_seats_dim1
given available_seats : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_legs)] of int
given delta_dim1, delta_dim2 : int
given delta : matrix indexed by [int(1..delta_dim1), int(1..delta_dim2)] of int
find packages_to_sell : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_packages)] of int(0..sum(demand))
find max_revenue : int(0..1000000000)

branching on [packages_to_sell]
maximising max_revenue
such that
$ the number of units sold of each package cannot exceed its estimated demand
forAll p : int(1..n_packages) . packages_to_sell[p] <= demand[p],
$ the seats reserved on each flight leg, summed over the packages that use the leg, cannot exceed the seats available on it
forAll l : int(1..n_legs) . (sum p : int(1..n_packages) . delta[p, l] * packages_to_sell[p]) <= available_seats[l],
$ the total revenue is the price of each package times the units sold, summed over the packages
max_revenue = (sum p : int(1..n_packages) . revenue[p] * packages_to_sell[p])
